1
00:00:14,994 --> 00:00:17,413
Why the hell are you doing this to me?

2
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:18,331
Why?

3
00:00:18,414 --> 00:00:20,542
"Why?" That's a bit hurtful.

4
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:21,918
I just

5
00:00:22,418 --> 00:00:24,087
want to be you.

6
00:00:25,171 --> 00:00:26,131
Do you understand?

7
00:00:40,186 --> 00:00:41,354
You are just

8
00:00:41,855 --> 00:00:43,148
jealous of me.

9
00:00:43,773 --> 00:00:47,110
You're dying of jealousy
because you want to be me.

10
00:00:47,193 --> 00:00:48,027
Aren't you?

11
00:00:50,613 --> 00:00:52,740
Shut up, you son of a bitch!

12
00:00:58,454 --> 00:00:59,330
This bastard

13
00:01:00,832 --> 00:01:02,208
isn't dead.

14
00:01:04,377 --> 00:01:05,503
He's still alive.

15
00:01:43,291 --> 00:01:46,294
MOUSETRAP

16
00:01:46,377 --> 00:01:49,297
You won the Best New Writer award
for Interview.

17
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:53,009
And you were even praised as a genius
after Evil Always Prevails.

18
00:01:53,092 --> 00:01:55,845
So what made you
suddenly go into seclusion?

19
00:01:56,471 --> 00:01:59,599
I think "seclusion"
might be a bit dramatic.

20
00:01:59,682 --> 00:02:00,850
How should I put this?

21
00:02:00,934 --> 00:02:02,977
A talentless writer

22
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:06,773
was floundering on blank pages

23
00:02:08,107 --> 00:02:12,028
and eventually realized
the well had run dry.

24
00:02:12,111 --> 00:02:16,241
When I was a third year in high school,
my parents passed away at the same time,

25
00:02:16,324 --> 00:02:18,534
and I went through
panic disorder afterward.

26
00:02:18,618 --> 00:02:20,870
-It was fine for a while.
-I see.

27
00:02:20,954 --> 00:02:24,540
Then it started again.

28
00:02:25,041 --> 00:02:27,835
I think it hit me pretty hard
at that time.

29
00:02:28,711 --> 00:02:30,296
I see.

30
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:33,591
So naturally, I guess
I started hiding from the world.

31
00:02:33,675 --> 00:02:36,344
Kind of like the rat in the book. Yeah.

32
00:02:42,475 --> 00:02:45,520
What the hell are you talking about?
He's not dead? So that's fake?

33
00:02:45,603 --> 00:02:48,648
You said that's his job.
The guy who said Yu-min was dead.

34
00:02:48,731 --> 00:02:50,566
Yeah, identity fraud.

35
00:02:52,527 --> 00:02:54,821
Damn, those fucking bastards…

36
00:02:54,904 --> 00:02:57,573
-Let's go. We have someone to meet.
-Who now?

37
00:02:58,783 --> 00:03:00,493
SAFER COMMUNITIES WITH DONGBU POLICE

38
00:03:03,329 --> 00:03:04,497
Man, it's hot.

39
00:03:05,748 --> 00:03:06,708
Hello.

40
00:03:07,583 --> 00:03:09,085
You're here.

41
00:03:09,168 --> 00:03:12,797
You didn't just show up with your novel
after all those years.

42
00:03:13,631 --> 00:03:15,466
You brought trouble too. Like your name.

43
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:16,843
Right.

44
00:03:16,926 --> 00:03:18,678
I'm sorry for the trouble.

45
00:03:18,761 --> 00:03:21,055
Oh, it's okay.
We've gotta catch the impersonator.

46
00:03:22,682 --> 00:03:25,935
But why this police station?
It's not even close to your place.

47
00:03:26,519 --> 00:03:27,645
Just because.

48
00:03:27,729 --> 00:03:29,814
It's a bigger police station.

49
00:03:33,067 --> 00:03:33,943
Right.

50
00:03:34,736 --> 00:03:37,905
Anyway, I'm sure our lawyer here
will take care of this.

51
00:03:38,406 --> 00:03:40,366
-All right, let's get in.
-Let's go.

52
00:03:42,994 --> 00:03:45,830
It gets so hot so quickly.

53
00:03:47,623 --> 00:03:50,626
Can we also request personal protection?

54
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:55,173
Did the impersonator threaten
or intimidate you?

55
00:03:55,757 --> 00:03:57,675
Not exactly.

56
00:03:58,885 --> 00:04:02,847
But I heard he showed up at my reunion
saying he was Je Moon-jae.

57
00:04:03,348 --> 00:04:04,640
And then,

58
00:04:04,724 --> 00:04:07,852
I heard one of my old classmates
died mysteriously.

59
00:04:07,935 --> 00:04:09,645
And his kid was kidnapped too.

60
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:12,482
-Oh, that case?
-Yes.

61
00:04:12,565 --> 00:04:14,984
How could your old classmates
mistake him for you?

62
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:17,779
I know, right? Well…

63
00:04:23,117 --> 00:04:25,328
They said he looked exactly

64
00:04:26,037 --> 00:04:27,372
like me.

65
00:04:28,581 --> 00:04:32,460
She was your editor-in-chief
when you got the Best New Writer award?

66
00:04:33,086 --> 00:04:36,047
Then why the hell is she publishing
a book with that rat bastard?

67
00:04:36,130 --> 00:04:39,425
How could she not tell the difference
between you and that rat bastard?

68
00:04:39,509 --> 00:04:41,511
We barely ever met.

69
00:04:41,594 --> 00:04:44,680
We mostly communicated by email,
so it's possible.

70
00:04:44,764 --> 00:04:47,725
It's because I'm a reclusive writer
who only uses a pen name.

71
00:04:47,809 --> 00:04:49,852
Did you fucking commit a crime or what?

72
00:04:49,936 --> 00:04:52,355
What are you, a thief?
Why hide your name? Damn it.

73
00:04:52,438 --> 00:04:54,190
That's just how writers…

74
00:04:55,858 --> 00:04:57,944
That's just how a lot of people are.

75
00:04:58,027 --> 00:04:59,987
But that bastard didn't use the pen name.

76
00:05:00,071 --> 00:05:02,156
He's using your actual name, Je Moon-jae.

77
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:04,200
Like he's the real Je Moon-jae.

78
00:05:04,283 --> 00:05:06,869
Come on.
Even his book's called The Rat. Fuck.

79
00:05:10,748 --> 00:05:11,582
Hey, by the way,

80
00:05:12,708 --> 00:05:14,669
how did the story end?

81
00:05:15,753 --> 00:05:18,089
You know the story. The old folklore.

82
00:05:18,172 --> 00:05:21,259
About a rat eating fingernails
and turning into a person.

83
00:05:21,342 --> 00:05:23,344
-Yeah.
-Yeah, you know…

84
00:05:23,428 --> 00:05:24,637
How did it end?

85
00:05:25,471 --> 00:05:26,639
It was…

86
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:29,851
a happy ending.

87
00:05:29,934 --> 00:05:30,935
Right? Damn it.

88
00:05:31,018 --> 00:05:32,937
Right? It's a happy ending, huh?

89
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:35,857
Not some fucked-up ending
or anything, right?

90
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:38,651
Yeah. Folklores are all about
good defeating evil.

91
00:05:45,116 --> 00:05:47,160
But are you sure you're the good guy?

92
00:05:49,996 --> 00:05:53,291
You look exactly like some bastard I know.

93
00:05:55,418 --> 00:05:56,252
Oh.

94
00:05:56,794 --> 00:05:59,172
I think you're saying

95
00:05:59,255 --> 00:06:01,299
I should prove that I'm Je Moon-jae.

96
00:06:03,342 --> 00:06:06,637
My publisher put out his book
when he won the Best New Writer award.

97
00:06:06,721 --> 00:06:07,930
I was the editor-in-chief.

98
00:06:08,556 --> 00:06:09,932
Right.

99
00:06:12,059 --> 00:06:14,896
Can two people really look that alike?
They're not even twins.

100
00:06:16,898 --> 00:06:17,732
Maybe

101
00:06:18,232 --> 00:06:20,776
he wanted to look like me

102
00:06:21,277 --> 00:06:23,070
because he wanted to steal my life.

103
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,198
Plastic surgery?

104
00:06:25,281 --> 00:06:29,660
Well, whether he got surgery or not,
he can't look exactly like me.

105
00:06:29,744 --> 00:06:33,039
I guess, if you look closely enough,
there have to be some differences.

106
00:06:37,710 --> 00:06:39,212
I don't care who's who.

107
00:06:40,171 --> 00:06:43,382
I just need to know who the killer is.
The bad guy.

108
00:06:45,343 --> 00:06:46,511
The bad guy?

109
00:06:50,473 --> 00:06:51,349
I don't know.

110
00:06:51,432 --> 00:06:53,184
I don't think there's a bad guy.

111
00:06:53,684 --> 00:06:55,811
I think there's only the survivor.

112
00:06:56,812 --> 00:07:00,191
I'm just saying
that's the situation he's creating.

113
00:07:03,277 --> 00:07:04,570
Is there anything else?

114
00:07:04,654 --> 00:07:05,488
Oh, right.

115
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:18,334
COMPLAINT

116
00:07:18,417 --> 00:07:20,294
COMPLAINANT: JE MOON-JAE
ACCUSED: JE MOON-JAE

117
00:07:23,673 --> 00:07:25,174
Hey, do you know me?

118
00:07:28,469 --> 00:07:31,597
Je Moon-jae. The name sounds familiar.

119
00:07:32,765 --> 00:07:34,058
Have we met before?

120
00:07:34,141 --> 00:07:36,102
The name rings a bell.

121
00:07:37,853 --> 00:07:39,146
No.

122
00:07:39,230 --> 00:07:41,983
-But why you?
-What?

123
00:07:42,066 --> 00:07:44,860
Why the hell is he so desperate
to take what's yours?

124
00:07:45,444 --> 00:07:47,780
Do you two know each other?

125
00:07:49,198 --> 00:07:53,286
I don't know.
I was wondering the same thing. Why me?

126
00:07:55,705 --> 00:07:57,707
Then what about me? Damn it.

127
00:07:57,790 --> 00:07:58,958
Why me?

128
00:08:00,209 --> 00:08:03,879
Why am I mixed up in your problem?

129
00:08:05,464 --> 00:08:07,592
There must be a police station
near your house.

130
00:08:07,675 --> 00:08:12,054
Why did you come all the way here
to file a complaint?

131
00:08:16,392 --> 00:08:18,561
I went to my friend's funeral

132
00:08:18,644 --> 00:08:21,522
and heard you guys
were investigating his case.

133
00:08:21,606 --> 00:08:25,818
I thought filing the complaint
at the same station might help.

134
00:08:25,901 --> 00:08:26,736
Doesn't that help?

135
00:08:33,242 --> 00:08:34,660
I'll get going now.

136
00:08:49,717 --> 00:08:50,593
Hey.

137
00:08:53,095 --> 00:08:54,597
This should be it.

138
00:08:55,389 --> 00:08:56,515
Did it move?

139
00:08:57,475 --> 00:08:59,310
NOVEL "THE RAT"

140
00:08:59,393 --> 00:09:01,437
Hey, it's Han Ji-hye, right?

141
00:09:01,937 --> 00:09:04,231
-The editor-in-chief of your first novel.
-Yeah.

142
00:09:04,732 --> 00:09:07,401
She started her own publishing house.
Damn it.

143
00:09:07,485 --> 00:09:09,278
You should've checked before coming.

144
00:09:10,363 --> 00:09:11,822
Damn.

145
00:09:11,906 --> 00:09:12,907
What now?

146
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:14,825
We go to this address, obviously.

147
00:09:15,409 --> 00:09:18,037
We also have to tell her
that bastard is deceiving her.

148
00:09:18,621 --> 00:09:20,289
Hey, who knows?

149
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:22,375
Maybe she'll be our cat.

150
00:09:25,169 --> 00:09:26,671
You know, in that story,

151
00:09:26,754 --> 00:09:29,757
the cat catches the rat that turned human.

152
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:33,928
The cat will probably know
who the fake one is.

153
00:09:35,262 --> 00:09:36,472
Let's go. Fuck.

154
00:09:36,972 --> 00:09:37,807
THE RAT

155
00:09:56,117 --> 00:09:56,951
What's wrong?

156
00:09:58,244 --> 00:09:59,412
Nothing, just…

157
00:10:00,121 --> 00:10:01,372
It feels unfamiliar.

158
00:10:01,872 --> 00:10:04,500
-What do you mean?
-You weren't like this before.

159
00:10:04,583 --> 00:10:08,546
You hated meeting people.
You hated coming to the publisher too.

160
00:10:10,089 --> 00:10:13,092
I only asked you to stay for coffee
out of courtesy.

161
00:10:13,175 --> 00:10:16,137
Yet here you are, having a cup of coffee.
I find it unfamiliar.

162
00:10:18,806 --> 00:10:20,474
Was I that bad?

163
00:10:20,558 --> 00:10:22,935
I guess your panic disorder
is all better now.

164
00:10:23,477 --> 00:10:24,353
That's good.

165
00:10:27,356 --> 00:10:28,315
Just a moment.

166
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:30,735
Hello?

167
00:10:32,236 --> 00:10:34,029
Is this Ms. Han, the editor-in-chief?

168
00:10:35,072 --> 00:10:38,284
You probably don't remember me.
This is Je Moon-jae.

169
00:10:41,162 --> 00:10:44,331
You helped me a lot
when I won the Best New Writer award.

170
00:10:46,375 --> 00:10:48,502
I have something to tell you in person.

171
00:10:49,170 --> 00:10:51,213
I saw the video of the book launch event.

172
00:10:51,297 --> 00:10:52,506
That wasn't me.

173
00:10:52,590 --> 00:10:54,675
That guy's deceiving you.

174
00:10:54,759 --> 00:10:56,594
Hey, um…

175
00:10:57,261 --> 00:10:58,888
He took everything from me

176
00:10:58,971 --> 00:11:01,223
while I was stuck at home
with a panic disorder.

177
00:11:01,307 --> 00:11:03,184
It's a bit complicated to explain.

178
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:05,144
I'm near the publisher right now.

179
00:11:05,227 --> 00:11:07,229
I'll explain everything in person.

180
00:11:07,313 --> 00:11:08,939
Could you spare me a few minutes?

181
00:11:27,166 --> 00:11:30,586
You're the only person
who can help me right now.

182
00:11:31,587 --> 00:11:33,839
Can you prove
you're really Mr. Je Moon-jae?

183
00:11:34,423 --> 00:11:36,342
You'll have to do it for me.

184
00:11:43,724 --> 00:11:46,060
The Rat. Did you write it yourself?

185
00:11:46,852 --> 00:11:48,646
No, I didn't write that.

186
00:11:48,729 --> 00:11:50,606
I think that guy wrote it.

187
00:11:50,689 --> 00:11:52,650
He used my childhood,

188
00:11:52,733 --> 00:11:55,236
the story of my parents' death,
and things like that.

189
00:11:55,319 --> 00:11:59,073
I think he used my whole life
as a motif in the story.

190
00:11:59,156 --> 00:12:00,908
It's a long story.

191
00:12:00,991 --> 00:12:04,662
-I think he knew me from before.
-Wait. Hold on.

192
00:12:07,331 --> 00:12:09,750
The person who wrote The Rat
is Je Moon-jae.

193
00:12:09,834 --> 00:12:11,126
I'm sure of that.

194
00:12:11,210 --> 00:12:14,004
People can lie, but the writings can't.

195
00:12:14,088 --> 00:12:16,090
I've read his books
since his very first one.

196
00:12:16,173 --> 00:12:19,093
You think the guy
who copied and stole my entire life

197
00:12:19,176 --> 00:12:21,011
couldn't imitate my writing?

198
00:12:21,095 --> 00:12:23,931
What happened to your panic disorder?
Are you all better now?

199
00:12:24,014 --> 00:12:25,057
No, I'm not.

200
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:27,935
With all this happening,
I had no choice but to come out.

201
00:12:28,018 --> 00:12:31,480
Je Moon-jae wouldn't even be sitting here.
Unless he's all better now.

202
00:12:31,564 --> 00:12:34,024
His panic disorder was really severe.

203
00:12:34,108 --> 00:12:36,277
That's what I'm saying here.

204
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:38,153
I may look fine on the outside,

205
00:12:38,737 --> 00:12:40,698
but I'm barely getting by on meds.

206
00:12:40,781 --> 00:12:42,366
This is for my panic disorder--

207
00:12:42,449 --> 00:12:44,702
-Get up. We have to go!
-Huh? Why?

208
00:12:44,785 --> 00:12:47,246
-Come on. Hurry.
-Why?

209
00:12:56,255 --> 00:12:59,383
-Did you get all the CCTV footage?
-No, I couldn't.

210
00:13:00,634 --> 00:13:02,636
Do you remember the suspect's appearance?

211
00:13:03,137 --> 00:13:04,096
Oh, there.

212
00:13:04,638 --> 00:13:05,472
Yeah.

213
00:13:07,266 --> 00:13:10,686
If something like this happened,
you should've called me.

214
00:13:10,769 --> 00:13:12,396
But instead, you called 112.

215
00:13:13,188 --> 00:13:15,065
This is driving me crazy. Seriously.

216
00:13:15,149 --> 00:13:18,611
Did you think he'd just show you his ID
if you asked for it?

217
00:13:19,194 --> 00:13:21,196
I wanted to check myself first.

218
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:24,992
I wasn't sure since he said
his panic disorder kept him stuck at home.

219
00:13:25,075 --> 00:13:27,828
Je Moon-jae
did have severe panic disorder.

220
00:13:29,747 --> 00:13:31,040
What's your conclusion?

221
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:32,958
Huh? This is the fake one?

222
00:13:34,001 --> 00:13:36,462
He was with the thug
from the picture you showed me.

223
00:13:36,545 --> 00:13:39,632
It would've been great
if you'd just let me catch him, you know?

224
00:13:40,132 --> 00:13:42,843
We're both busy people.
No need to waste our time like this.

225
00:13:42,927 --> 00:13:44,470
I fully understand.

226
00:13:44,553 --> 00:13:47,473
I'll call you if he contacts me again.

227
00:13:47,556 --> 00:13:49,892
Just catch that scammer who ran off.

228
00:13:51,310 --> 00:13:52,227
Look.

229
00:13:56,523 --> 00:13:58,359
He's not a scammer.

230
00:13:58,901 --> 00:14:00,110
He's a murderer.

231
00:14:01,654 --> 00:14:03,447
Yes, whatever he is.

232
00:14:11,330 --> 00:14:14,124
He was stuck at home
because of his panic disorder?

233
00:14:14,875 --> 00:14:17,044
KIDNAPPING CASE
FATHER FOUND DEAD IN THE HANGANG RIVER

234
00:14:17,127 --> 00:14:18,420
SUSPECT LINKED TO SHOOTING CASE

235
00:14:22,883 --> 00:14:24,760
Not one bastard is helping.

236
00:14:25,386 --> 00:14:27,972
Everywhere I look,
there are just damn enemies!

237
00:14:29,056 --> 00:14:30,265
You bastard!

238
00:14:30,349 --> 00:14:33,143
What the hell have you been doing
to cause this mess?

239
00:14:33,227 --> 00:14:34,186
I don't know!

240
00:14:34,269 --> 00:14:37,439
How the hell can I tell you anything
when I don't know what's going on?

241
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:39,942
No one is telling me a damn thing!

242
00:14:40,943 --> 00:14:42,611
How can I prove I'm really me?

243
00:14:42,695 --> 00:14:45,614
Can you prove you're you?
How would you do that?

244
00:14:46,115 --> 00:14:48,867
You fucking bastard!

245
00:14:49,368 --> 00:14:53,664
You need others to prove it, punk!
They know me better than I do.

246
00:14:53,747 --> 00:14:55,874
But why doesn't that work for you, punk?

247
00:14:55,958 --> 00:14:57,710
Why can't anyone prove it for you?!

248
00:14:57,793 --> 00:14:58,836
You bastard!

249
00:15:03,632 --> 00:15:05,092
Fuck!

250
00:15:12,057 --> 00:15:13,684
Forget proving it.

251
00:15:14,685 --> 00:15:16,520
We have to lay low first.

252
00:15:25,946 --> 00:15:28,073
What do you want me to do with him?

253
00:15:28,574 --> 00:15:30,325
Look into him.

254
00:15:30,409 --> 00:15:32,619
Dig up everything about him.

255
00:15:34,496 --> 00:15:38,917
Turn over every rock to find out
if that bastard really is Je Moon-jae.

256
00:15:40,544 --> 00:15:41,628
Yeah.

257
00:15:41,712 --> 00:15:43,672
He never caused trouble
while he lived here.

258
00:15:43,756 --> 00:15:45,966
He was always the first to say hello.

259
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:49,011
Like I said before, he did live here.

260
00:15:50,345 --> 00:15:52,598
He's the guy who lives in this building.

261
00:15:52,681 --> 00:15:54,767
He got takeout
three or four times a month.

262
00:15:54,850 --> 00:15:56,477
It's the Heineken guy.

263
00:15:56,560 --> 00:16:00,147
Once a week, every Friday,
four cans of Heineken.

264
00:16:03,734 --> 00:16:07,488
Doesn't sound like someone
who stayed holed up with panic disorder.

265
00:16:31,136 --> 00:16:32,805
We received a tip.

266
00:16:45,359 --> 00:16:48,529
Can two people really look that alike?
They're not even twins.

267
00:16:48,612 --> 00:16:49,446
Maybe

268
00:16:49,947 --> 00:16:52,741
he wanted to look like me

269
00:16:53,992 --> 00:16:56,161
because he wanted to steal my life.

270
00:16:57,204 --> 00:16:58,914
Which one is it?

271
00:17:06,255 --> 00:17:10,926
So you're asking where I was
the first week of this month?

272
00:17:12,344 --> 00:17:15,973
That might be difficult for me to prove.

273
00:17:16,056 --> 00:17:18,475
Nobody remembers when it hurts them.

274
00:17:18,559 --> 00:17:19,935
Is this one of those cases?

275
00:17:20,018 --> 00:17:21,395
No, it's not that.

276
00:17:21,895 --> 00:17:25,524
That was right before my book came out,
so I was alone.

277
00:17:25,607 --> 00:17:27,442
There's no one who can vouch for me.

278
00:17:28,902 --> 00:17:30,112
Where were you?

279
00:17:30,195 --> 00:17:31,238
At a vacation home.

280
00:17:31,321 --> 00:17:34,867
It was right before my book came out,
so I wanted to focus on my writing.

281
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:37,369
But why are you suspecting me?

282
00:17:37,452 --> 00:17:38,537
I'm the victim.

283
00:17:39,788 --> 00:17:43,041
Comes with the job.
That's how I make a living.

284
00:17:43,125 --> 00:17:45,294
Either way, one of you is a fake.

285
00:17:45,377 --> 00:17:48,755
Just give me your alibi already
so you can walk free.

286
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:52,134
Then I'll send you a link.
It has the rental's address.

287
00:17:52,217 --> 00:17:53,719
You can check it out.

288
00:17:54,219 --> 00:17:55,053
Well…

289
00:17:55,721 --> 00:17:56,680
Hello?

290
00:17:57,681 --> 00:17:58,682
Hello?

291
00:18:00,434 --> 00:18:02,686
This bastard, seriously. Damn it.

292
00:18:11,278 --> 00:18:14,531
SKY SOUND VACATION HOME

293
00:18:14,615 --> 00:18:17,743
He's the man in the photo you sent.

294
00:18:17,826 --> 00:18:19,870
About ten days?

295
00:18:19,953 --> 00:18:23,373
Yes, he stayed for about ten days.

296
00:18:28,337 --> 00:18:31,215
He was on his laptop whenever I saw him.

297
00:18:32,633 --> 00:18:35,427
His car was parked in the lot
for the entire ten days.

298
00:18:35,510 --> 00:18:38,347
There's so much to do around here,
but he never went out.

299
00:18:39,306 --> 00:18:41,058
I think he was a writer.

300
00:18:41,141 --> 00:18:46,146
I checked the CCTV footage just in case,
and it really was him.

301
00:18:50,609 --> 00:18:52,194
Then was it you?

302
00:19:19,972 --> 00:19:23,350
Let's go. If the locals see us,
they'll get suspicious.

303
00:19:24,059 --> 00:19:25,894
-Did you sleep?
-Sort of.

304
00:19:26,687 --> 00:19:29,564
I must be getting old.
Fuck. I can't sleep in the car anymore.

305
00:19:43,912 --> 00:19:46,123
Maybe I should see
the editor-in-chief again.

306
00:19:46,623 --> 00:19:49,793
I couldn't tell her everything last time.
Should I call her?

307
00:19:54,256 --> 00:19:56,508
You look at me like my father did.

308
00:19:56,591 --> 00:19:58,385
How did he look at you?

309
00:19:58,468 --> 00:19:59,928
Like I was pathetic.

310
00:20:00,012 --> 00:20:01,471
What pathetic thing did you do?

311
00:20:02,639 --> 00:20:04,224
I don't know. He never told me.

312
00:20:05,017 --> 00:20:08,395
He looked at me like he knew everything
and I knew nothing.

313
00:20:08,895 --> 00:20:11,106
He'd been that way since I was a kid.

314
00:20:11,189 --> 00:20:13,817
Like he knew everything about the world.

315
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:15,986
I bet he didn't even know
he'd die like that.

316
00:20:18,113 --> 00:20:19,740
That's how I'm looking at you.

317
00:20:22,451 --> 00:20:24,953
If we go see the editor-in-chief again,
we'll get caught.

318
00:20:25,454 --> 00:20:27,039
It's a pathetic and stupid thing to do.

319
00:20:28,290 --> 00:20:30,625
I don't get it.
How could she believe that bastard?

320
00:20:31,293 --> 00:20:32,127
Hey.

321
00:20:32,627 --> 00:20:35,672
He wrote a novel himself.
Maybe he's a better writer than you.

322
00:20:36,256 --> 00:20:38,050
Think of something while we lay low.

323
00:20:38,133 --> 00:20:39,843
Something only you have.

324
00:20:39,926 --> 00:20:43,263
Something he doesn't know and can't get.
Your very own alibi.

325
00:20:43,889 --> 00:20:44,931
Prove it with that.

326
00:20:51,855 --> 00:20:53,857
You said I'd get promoted, punk.

327
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:58,737
-So you agreed to hand it to Major Crimes?
-What choice do I have?

328
00:20:59,237 --> 00:21:01,573
A tip, murder, and identity fraud.
The full package.

329
00:21:01,656 --> 00:21:05,202
We busted our asses for this,
and now Major Crimes gets all the credit.

330
00:21:05,702 --> 00:21:08,497
But sir, this is great.

331
00:21:08,997 --> 00:21:12,793
It's better not to get involved
with headache cases. Yes.

332
00:21:13,585 --> 00:21:15,796
-Am I wrong?
-You're right.

333
00:21:16,463 --> 00:21:18,382
So you should drop it too.

334
00:21:18,882 --> 00:21:20,342
Drop the case, got it?

335
00:21:20,425 --> 00:21:23,220
I got it. I'll stop.
I already handed over the files.

336
00:21:24,137 --> 00:21:25,055
Really?

337
00:21:25,847 --> 00:21:27,182
Yes, really.

338
00:21:27,265 --> 00:21:28,558
You really need to stop.

339
00:21:29,684 --> 00:21:32,479
Have you been lied to your whole life?
I said I got it.

340
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:35,565
You're not gonna stop, punk!

341
00:22:01,383 --> 00:22:04,469
Oh man. It's only been a few days,
and you already look…

342
00:22:05,178 --> 00:22:08,723
You might rot away
after a few years inside.

343
00:22:10,767 --> 00:22:13,103
Your real boss, Park Seung-gyu.

344
00:22:13,186 --> 00:22:16,481
He bolted overseas by himself
before the travel ban kicked in.

345
00:22:17,566 --> 00:22:18,817
It was quick. So quick.

346
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:20,444
It was insanely quick.

347
00:22:21,361 --> 00:22:24,239
Major Crimes is taking over the case.
What are you gonna do?

348
00:22:24,322 --> 00:22:26,199
You're the only one who's screwed.

349
00:22:27,909 --> 00:22:30,871
Well, that thing
you were hiding in your shop.

350
00:22:30,954 --> 00:22:33,957
That cash box. What happened to it?

351
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:35,500
It was empty.

352
00:22:36,251 --> 00:22:40,797
You thought you could do a few years
and live off your hidden cash?

353
00:22:41,548 --> 00:22:42,966
Understandable, yeah.

354
00:22:44,009 --> 00:22:45,844
I would've thought so too.

355
00:22:45,927 --> 00:22:47,637
Wait. Why am I here?

356
00:22:47,721 --> 00:22:48,597
Right.

357
00:22:49,347 --> 00:22:51,349
I've got something to ask you.

358
00:22:51,433 --> 00:22:52,934
Kwak Sang-cheol.

359
00:22:55,061 --> 00:22:56,146
Do you know him?

360
00:22:56,646 --> 00:23:01,568
I looked into the gang that Noja was in,
and I found this guy there.

361
00:23:01,651 --> 00:23:05,822
He killed someone
and ran off to the Philippines.

362
00:23:05,906 --> 00:23:08,867
Look here.
This one's a real vicious bastard.

363
00:23:09,659 --> 00:23:10,577
Do you know him?

364
00:23:12,329 --> 00:23:13,705
MURDER
KWAK SANG-CHEOL (43)

365
00:23:13,788 --> 00:23:15,874
Wait. What's this?

366
00:23:18,001 --> 00:23:20,545
Why does this bastard look like you?

367
00:23:21,046 --> 00:23:22,130
What the hell?

368
00:23:22,214 --> 00:23:23,465
Why do you two look alike?

369
00:23:24,466 --> 00:23:27,010
Huh? You really do look like him.

370
00:23:28,053 --> 00:23:29,137
I get it now.

371
00:23:30,889 --> 00:23:32,349
That's right. Park Seung-gyu.

372
00:23:32,933 --> 00:23:35,060
He runs an identity fraud ring.

373
00:23:35,143 --> 00:23:37,187
So this means

374
00:23:38,146 --> 00:23:39,564
that bastard

375
00:23:40,190 --> 00:23:43,985
might have turned this bastard
into this bastard.

376
00:23:54,287 --> 00:23:55,580
You fucking bastard.

377
00:23:56,164 --> 00:23:58,792
If the prosecution finds out
you're Kwak Sang-cheol,

378
00:23:59,376 --> 00:24:02,212
you won't be celebrating
your 70th birthday outside.

379
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:07,926
Sang-cheol, you know what?

380
00:24:09,803 --> 00:24:11,846
I'm the only one who knows about this.

381
00:24:17,102 --> 00:24:21,314
Fuck. The pigs even cleaned this out.

382
00:24:21,398 --> 00:24:23,400
We busted our asses just to pay taxes.

383
00:24:23,483 --> 00:24:26,194
Sir, I already sent someone abroad
using your ID.

384
00:24:26,278 --> 00:24:27,779
You should get changed now.

385
00:24:27,862 --> 00:24:29,322
But this…

386
00:24:29,906 --> 00:24:31,825
The pigs didn't take this.

387
00:24:32,576 --> 00:24:36,663
The pigs love showing off.
They'd have leaked this already.

388
00:24:37,914 --> 00:24:42,419
Those bastards are just civil servants
who'd do anything for a promotion.

389
00:24:52,762 --> 00:24:53,805
So…

390
00:24:56,349 --> 00:24:58,310
Myeong-su's the one who took it.

391
00:25:00,103 --> 00:25:03,481
He was probably the fucking one
who sent the tip too.

392
00:25:03,982 --> 00:25:08,653
That bastard has multiple names
and identities.

393
00:25:08,737 --> 00:25:11,698
Fake identities that pay taxes
and get regular checkups.

394
00:25:12,282 --> 00:25:16,620
Seung-gyu used to find places
for the wanted higher-ups to hide

395
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:19,456
and make fake identities for them.

396
00:25:19,956 --> 00:25:23,418
And then
he turned identity fraud into a business.

397
00:25:23,501 --> 00:25:25,420
He caught the higher-ups' attention.

398
00:25:25,503 --> 00:25:28,381
And he branched out
into online gambling and loan sharking.

399
00:25:28,465 --> 00:25:30,425
That puny runt's come a long way.

400
00:25:31,843 --> 00:25:35,305
The guy who left the country?
No way that was really Seung-gyu.

401
00:25:35,805 --> 00:25:38,850
He would never leave the country
without fixing this problem.

402
00:25:38,933 --> 00:25:39,768
What problem?

403
00:25:39,851 --> 00:25:41,645
The tip.

404
00:25:41,728 --> 00:25:43,521
But your names aren't on the tip.

405
00:25:43,605 --> 00:25:45,732
We're all tangled up in this.

406
00:25:45,815 --> 00:25:48,943
If you dig into our pasts,
we're all connected somehow.

407
00:25:49,027 --> 00:25:51,363
Seung-gyu has to kill
everyone connected to the tip.

408
00:25:51,446 --> 00:25:52,906
Why?

409
00:25:52,989 --> 00:25:56,034
If Noja or I open our mouths,
he's screwed.

410
00:25:56,618 --> 00:26:00,372
He threw away countless empty shells
after taking what was inside.

411
00:26:00,455 --> 00:26:01,665
Is that why you sent it?

412
00:26:01,748 --> 00:26:04,668
So you could screw everyone over
and be the sole survivor?

413
00:26:06,044 --> 00:26:09,839
It had to be someone
who knew more about this than I did.

414
00:26:11,216 --> 00:26:12,509
And who's that?

415
00:26:15,553 --> 00:26:16,888
Do you have a cigarette?

416
00:26:17,972 --> 00:26:19,307
Yeah, I've got one.

417
00:26:32,028 --> 00:26:35,657
We were all doing fine before this, right?

418
00:26:36,866 --> 00:26:40,286
This is all because of that bastard.
He must've sent the tip too.

419
00:26:40,370 --> 00:26:41,538
That bastard?

420
00:26:42,122 --> 00:26:42,956
Who?

421
00:26:45,875 --> 00:26:47,919
The guy who should've died
and disappeared.

422
00:26:48,420 --> 00:26:51,047
Everything went to shit
because he came back from the dead.

423
00:27:31,546 --> 00:27:32,380
Yeah.

424
00:27:34,174 --> 00:27:35,133
So?

425
00:27:35,842 --> 00:27:36,885
What?

426
00:27:37,510 --> 00:27:41,097
Goddamn it. Bring me something solid.

427
00:27:41,598 --> 00:27:42,599
Something irrefutable.

428
00:27:46,644 --> 00:27:47,812
Who was it?

429
00:27:49,731 --> 00:27:51,065
None of your business.

430
00:27:52,942 --> 00:27:55,153
Where are we? Where are we going?

431
00:27:55,236 --> 00:27:57,739
A good place to lay low.

432
00:27:58,573 --> 00:28:00,116
Near my hometown.

433
00:28:02,368 --> 00:28:06,748
Isn't it risky going back to your hometown
with the cops after us?

434
00:28:08,208 --> 00:28:10,877
Maybe it's because my life
is about to be over,

435
00:28:12,045 --> 00:28:13,546
but I miss my hometown.

436
00:28:16,132 --> 00:28:17,258
Who's there?

437
00:28:20,220 --> 00:28:21,262
The proof

438
00:28:21,930 --> 00:28:23,765
that I'm really me.

439
00:28:26,142 --> 00:28:27,644
Hey, when we get there,

440
00:28:27,727 --> 00:28:31,898
hide for a few days
and think about who you really are.

441
00:28:33,066 --> 00:28:35,610
Just sit alone in the middle of the night

442
00:28:36,110 --> 00:28:39,364
and think about
what kind of bastard you are.

443
00:28:39,447 --> 00:28:42,784
And think about how there's no one
who can prove who you really are.

444
00:28:43,868 --> 00:28:46,412
You no-good bastard.

445
00:28:47,997 --> 00:28:49,040
Damn it.

446
00:29:05,723 --> 00:29:09,477
The cars sound like
the waves in the ocean.

447
00:29:10,478 --> 00:29:12,897
The sound of waves
in the middle of the city.

448
00:29:12,981 --> 00:29:16,109
I envy your senses.

449
00:29:21,990 --> 00:29:25,368
By the way, when are you finishing
the second volume?

450
00:29:25,451 --> 00:29:28,329
It should come out
while the first volume's still hot.

451
00:29:28,830 --> 00:29:30,331
How come

452
00:29:30,415 --> 00:29:32,709
you showed up so suddenly
without telling me?

453
00:29:34,419 --> 00:29:35,253
Oh.

454
00:29:35,753 --> 00:29:39,007
I was just passing by.
I was curious about the second volume too.

455
00:29:39,507 --> 00:29:40,383
Come on.

456
00:29:40,466 --> 00:29:42,594
You left in a hurry
after that call yesterday.

457
00:29:42,677 --> 00:29:44,137
So I thought you were busy,

458
00:29:44,220 --> 00:29:45,847
but I guess not.

459
00:29:46,764 --> 00:29:49,434
Come on, tell me. Why did you really come?

460
00:29:49,517 --> 00:29:51,227
Not about the second volume, right?

461
00:29:52,645 --> 00:29:54,898
No, I really came to ask about it.

462
00:29:54,981 --> 00:29:58,067
It's good. When will you finish it?

463
00:29:59,485 --> 00:30:00,403
Come on.

464
00:30:01,738 --> 00:30:03,281
My writing…

465
00:30:08,828 --> 00:30:10,788
Still doubting me after reading it?

466
00:30:16,127 --> 00:30:17,211
I mean…

467
00:30:18,129 --> 00:30:20,423
Things don't always go as planned, huh?

468
00:30:23,301 --> 00:30:26,137
I guess I dropped by too suddenly, right?

469
00:30:26,220 --> 00:30:27,680
Just hold on.

470
00:30:28,181 --> 00:30:29,265
Right now, I'm…

471
00:30:29,766 --> 00:30:31,100
Well,

472
00:30:31,851 --> 00:30:33,561
I'm at a crossroads.

473
00:30:33,645 --> 00:30:38,316
And I'm not entirely sure what to choose.
Could you give me some time?

474
00:30:53,331 --> 00:30:55,041
The guy who should've died
and disappeared.

475
00:30:55,124 --> 00:30:57,627
Everything went to shit
because he came back from the dead.

476
00:31:10,139 --> 00:31:11,474
Let's help each other out.

477
00:31:12,725 --> 00:31:15,144
You don't want to live
as the front either.

478
00:31:17,438 --> 00:31:19,524
I've got a plan.

479
00:31:21,943 --> 00:31:22,944
Do you wanna hear it?

480
00:31:25,488 --> 00:31:29,033
That bastard learned some bad shit
while he was held by Seung-gyu.

481
00:31:29,742 --> 00:31:33,204
He killed a homeless guy
and committed identity fraud.

482
00:31:33,287 --> 00:31:34,247
How?

483
00:31:34,330 --> 00:31:36,040
How did you help him?

484
00:31:36,124 --> 00:31:38,001
I made him a dead man.

485
00:31:38,501 --> 00:31:41,170
I've got a guy I know
at a public hospital morgue.

486
00:31:41,254 --> 00:31:42,922
He was in some gambling debt.

487
00:31:44,424 --> 00:31:47,427
We cremated the homeless guy
under this punk's name.

488
00:31:47,510 --> 00:31:49,846
And he disappeared for a while.

489
00:31:50,596 --> 00:31:52,807
Then he showed up the other day.

490
00:31:53,516 --> 00:31:55,018
And his face had changed.

491
00:31:55,518 --> 00:31:57,020
This bastard

492
00:31:57,603 --> 00:31:58,938
became this bastard.

493
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:00,898
And he called himself the Rat.

494
00:32:00,982 --> 00:32:03,359
He started talking complete horse crap

495
00:32:03,443 --> 00:32:07,030
about petty jealousy creating a monster.

496
00:32:10,616 --> 00:32:11,701
What bullshit is that?

497
00:32:11,784 --> 00:32:14,037
Exactly. Why the hell should I care?

498
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:17,790
I just wanted to quit being the front
and live a decent life.

499
00:32:17,874 --> 00:32:21,169
He came to me saying
I'd better get in shape for prison.

500
00:32:22,086 --> 00:32:24,005
He said I'd be rich after a year or two.

501
00:32:24,839 --> 00:32:26,591
Can you tell them apart?

502
00:32:27,425 --> 00:32:28,760
Well, that depends on

503
00:32:29,427 --> 00:32:32,764
whether we can make a deal, doesn't it?

504
00:32:33,264 --> 00:32:34,891
NAME: SEO YU-MIN

505
00:33:01,459 --> 00:33:03,127
The Rat…

506
00:34:08,442 --> 00:34:11,529
Noja, you know the picture you sent me?

507
00:34:12,029 --> 00:34:14,532
The girl. The one with the tattoo.

508
00:34:15,199 --> 00:34:16,409
She died.

509
00:34:16,492 --> 00:34:18,995
I checked the CCTV footage.

510
00:34:19,579 --> 00:34:21,622
And the suspect is…

511
00:34:22,498 --> 00:34:23,749
It's him.

512
00:34:24,959 --> 00:34:27,003
His father was a writer too.

513
00:34:27,086 --> 00:34:29,172
So I started digging into his father,

514
00:34:29,255 --> 00:34:31,966
and I found some shocking evidence.

515
00:34:52,403 --> 00:34:55,573
Why did you take so long
to go to a convenience store?

516
00:35:06,542 --> 00:35:09,587
Are we even allowed to be here?
We didn't get permission.

517
00:35:11,672 --> 00:35:12,715
This is

518
00:35:14,050 --> 00:35:16,552
where a married monk I know used to live.

519
00:35:17,803 --> 00:35:20,723
He opened a small prayer hall in town
and stopped coming here.

520
00:35:21,641 --> 00:35:23,309
Can you even sleep here?

521
00:35:25,686 --> 00:35:28,147
I guess your life's not tiring enough.

522
00:35:31,692 --> 00:35:33,945
I don't know. I'm hungry.

523
00:35:40,952 --> 00:35:42,453
Let me ask you something.

524
00:35:43,454 --> 00:35:44,330
What?

525
00:35:47,166 --> 00:35:49,001
Where were you early this month?

526
00:35:50,795 --> 00:35:53,422
What do you mean? I was home.

527
00:35:57,969 --> 00:36:00,888
I told you.
I didn't leave my house for three years.

528
00:36:01,722 --> 00:36:02,848
Why?

529
00:36:03,432 --> 00:36:06,936
Is there anyone who can prove
that you never left home?

530
00:36:08,062 --> 00:36:09,272
There used to be.

531
00:36:10,106 --> 00:36:11,983
But he died. Soo-hyun.

532
00:36:12,692 --> 00:36:13,901
Oh, right.

533
00:36:14,986 --> 00:36:16,445
So there's no one now?

534
00:36:22,827 --> 00:36:24,245
Why?

535
00:36:25,288 --> 00:36:27,415
The girl who was with you and the Rat.

536
00:36:28,374 --> 00:36:30,668
-The one with the ankle tattoo.
-Yeah.

537
00:36:31,252 --> 00:36:32,086
She died.

538
00:36:36,757 --> 00:36:38,301
But how did she die?

539
00:36:39,760 --> 00:36:41,178
You killed her.

540
00:36:43,347 --> 00:36:44,181
Huh?

541
00:36:44,265 --> 00:36:47,059
The police got the CCTV footage
from the crime scene.

542
00:36:47,143 --> 00:36:48,477
And you were there.

543
00:36:52,023 --> 00:36:52,857
Then

544
00:36:53,816 --> 00:36:55,609
it must've been that bastard.

545
00:36:55,693 --> 00:36:57,528
I never left home. How could I kill her?

546
00:36:57,611 --> 00:36:59,488
The police files say

547
00:36:59,572 --> 00:37:01,157
tons of people saw you

548
00:37:01,240 --> 00:37:04,744
around the apartment
you were supposedly hiding in, bastard.

549
00:37:04,827 --> 00:37:08,164
How did a bastard who never left home
buy beer every week?

550
00:37:08,247 --> 00:37:10,499
Then that must also be that bastard…

551
00:37:12,251 --> 00:37:14,128
Noja, do you suspect me?

552
00:37:14,211 --> 00:37:15,254
Yeah.

553
00:37:27,975 --> 00:37:29,143
JE GEUN-U
CRITICS AWARD WINNER

554
00:37:30,144 --> 00:37:31,771
They're your parents, right?

555
00:37:31,854 --> 00:37:33,898
Je Geun-u. Han Yeong-hui.

556
00:37:34,732 --> 00:37:37,193
Wow, the whole family
turned up for his award.

557
00:37:37,693 --> 00:37:38,903
But…

558
00:37:38,986 --> 00:37:39,987
What's this?

559
00:37:40,738 --> 00:37:42,114
Is that you?

560
00:37:44,075 --> 00:37:45,326
That's not you, is it?

561
00:37:47,620 --> 00:37:48,496
Hey.

562
00:37:50,247 --> 00:37:51,957
Who are you? You fucking asshole.

563
00:37:54,043 --> 00:37:57,380
After I entered the Buddhist path,

564
00:37:57,880 --> 00:38:03,052
I was taught that attachment
is the root of suffering.

565
00:38:03,844 --> 00:38:07,932
What future are you so desperate to know
that you came all this way?

566
00:38:08,724 --> 00:38:09,725
Noja.

567
00:38:11,519 --> 00:38:13,020
Where's Noja right now?

568
00:38:13,729 --> 00:38:15,898
Who is Noja?

569
00:38:22,822 --> 00:38:24,240
Your junior from high school.

570
00:38:25,032 --> 00:38:26,700
The guy who set this up for you.

571
00:38:28,911 --> 00:38:30,996
I think

572
00:38:31,580 --> 00:38:35,793
you might have come here by mistake.

573
00:38:41,924 --> 00:38:43,968
Isn't this photoshopped?

574
00:38:44,051 --> 00:38:45,761
It's a screenshot, punk.

575
00:38:46,262 --> 00:38:49,014
That picture was in a magazine
called Literary Review.

576
00:38:49,098 --> 00:38:51,142
They're your parents, right?

577
00:38:51,225 --> 00:38:52,226
They are, but…

578
00:38:52,309 --> 00:38:56,188
That was issued
a year before you were born.

579
00:38:56,272 --> 00:38:59,650
But, fuck, that's Je Moon-jae there,
all grown up.

580
00:39:00,651 --> 00:39:01,485
No.

581
00:39:01,569 --> 00:39:06,073
My parents said they had me late
because they struggled to have a kid.

582
00:39:07,158 --> 00:39:08,284
Who is this kid?

583
00:39:09,076 --> 00:39:10,911
It says Je Moon-jae. You bastard!

584
00:39:13,998 --> 00:39:15,541
I'll ask you again.

585
00:39:17,293 --> 00:39:18,961
Just answer my question.

586
00:39:19,753 --> 00:39:21,255
Who are you, you bastard?

587
00:39:27,178 --> 00:39:31,348
MANBULAM

588
00:39:39,773 --> 00:39:41,233
FOUND HIM

589
00:39:49,909 --> 00:39:53,746
Why the fuck are you giving me
this shit too?

590
00:39:53,829 --> 00:39:56,081
You can't explain anything right now,
you bastard!

591
00:39:56,165 --> 00:39:57,249
Explain how?

592
00:39:58,375 --> 00:40:00,794
How do I explain that I'm me?

593
00:40:03,547 --> 00:40:06,509
You said when your parents died,

594
00:40:06,592 --> 00:40:09,178
you handled the funeral alone
because you had no relatives.

595
00:40:09,261 --> 00:40:12,515
But it looks like you have an uncle.

596
00:40:14,892 --> 00:40:15,726
Huh?

597
00:40:18,145 --> 00:40:19,730
Now you don't even remember that?

598
00:40:20,314 --> 00:40:21,440
What uncle?

599
00:40:23,192 --> 00:40:24,276
I don't have an uncle.

600
00:40:28,864 --> 00:40:31,492
When we track down bastards
who skip out on loans,

601
00:40:31,575 --> 00:40:34,495
we dig up everything,
even all their relatives and their exes.

602
00:40:34,578 --> 00:40:36,997
That's what makes us
more competent than the police.

603
00:40:40,042 --> 00:40:41,752
Get up, you fucking bastard.

604
00:40:49,009 --> 00:40:51,178
I'll have you meet
the uncle you never had.

605
00:40:51,262 --> 00:40:55,140
If you're not Je Moon-jae there either,

606
00:40:56,600 --> 00:40:59,311
you're really fucking dead.

607
00:41:15,744 --> 00:41:17,705
If I'm not Je Moon-jae, then what am I?

608
00:41:18,998 --> 00:41:21,250
Why the hell are you asking me,
you bastard?

609
00:41:22,042 --> 00:41:25,462
A kidnapper, a murderer…

610
00:41:26,213 --> 00:41:28,841
You really think
that I'm this nameless rat?

611
00:41:31,552 --> 00:41:33,554
What if this uncle guy can't prove it?

612
00:41:33,637 --> 00:41:34,972
I told you.

613
00:41:35,472 --> 00:41:36,473
You'll fucking die.

614
00:41:38,183 --> 00:41:40,561
No, that's not what I meant.

615
00:41:42,771 --> 00:41:46,442
Even if I die,
I should at least have a name.

616
00:41:47,109 --> 00:41:48,986
Who am I gonna die as?

617
00:41:49,570 --> 00:41:50,529
When you die?

618
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:52,573
You don't need a name.

619
00:41:52,656 --> 00:41:55,659
You only need a name when you're alive.

620
00:41:59,788 --> 00:42:03,083
If I had an uncle, the rat bastard
probably took care of that too.

621
00:42:04,460 --> 00:42:07,087
That's how things have been so far.
Don't you get it yet?

622
00:42:07,171 --> 00:42:09,923
Shut up and just come, punk.
I just wanna know!

623
00:42:11,175 --> 00:42:13,177
What kind of bastard you really are.

624
00:42:47,044 --> 00:42:51,507
Should've told the guy not to kill him.
We should bury him alive.

625
00:42:51,590 --> 00:42:53,592
And give him some noja money.

626
00:42:56,053 --> 00:42:58,222
I still can't forget Dong-seok's eyes

627
00:42:59,014 --> 00:43:01,016
when he was buried.

628
00:43:03,644 --> 00:43:05,854
But why was he buried?

629
00:43:07,272 --> 00:43:08,565
Jealousy, what else?

630
00:43:09,566 --> 00:43:12,945
Noja was the capable one,
but Dong-seok was the one who made it big.

631
00:43:13,028 --> 00:43:17,199
That must've rubbed him the wrong way.
He was acting superior to him.

632
00:43:17,282 --> 00:43:20,911
Jealousy. It's a scary thing.

633
00:43:20,994 --> 00:43:22,037
Hey.

634
00:43:22,538 --> 00:43:25,165
Tell him not to kill Noja.
I'll give him a bonus for it.

635
00:43:25,666 --> 00:43:26,959
Yes, got it.

636
00:43:27,626 --> 00:43:29,503
I have to bury him alive.

637
00:43:30,003 --> 00:43:31,213
Just like Dong-seok.

638
00:44:02,619 --> 00:44:03,704
Bastard!

639
00:44:29,938 --> 00:44:31,815
Hey. Are you okay?

640
00:45:05,307 --> 00:45:06,934
Goddamn it.

641
00:45:07,518 --> 00:45:08,560
Hey, punk.

642
00:45:12,564 --> 00:45:13,398
Get on my back.

643
00:45:13,482 --> 00:45:14,817
For fuck's sake.

644
00:45:15,776 --> 00:45:17,069
Fucking hell.

645
00:45:19,696 --> 00:45:20,864
Fuck.

646
00:45:32,584 --> 00:45:34,336
You fucking bastard!

647
00:45:50,269 --> 00:45:52,896
What is going on this late at night?

648
00:45:53,730 --> 00:45:57,150
I'm calling to report gunshots
at Manbulam.

649
00:46:15,127 --> 00:46:16,461
Fuck.

650
00:46:18,714 --> 00:46:21,133
Fucking idiot. You didn't even know
you were shot! Damn it.

651
00:46:23,051 --> 00:46:24,970
Stay awake
until we get to the hospital, punk!

652
00:46:25,596 --> 00:46:28,432
Noja. We can't go to the hospital now.

653
00:46:29,516 --> 00:46:32,728
If we get caught,
we'll take the fall for everything.

654
00:46:32,811 --> 00:46:35,022
That's better than dying, you dumbass!

655
00:46:35,606 --> 00:46:36,982
If I get caught now,

656
00:46:38,567 --> 00:46:40,777
am I supposed to live as the Rat forever?

657
00:46:44,907 --> 00:46:46,199
Hey.

658
00:46:46,283 --> 00:46:47,868
Fuck.

659
00:46:54,666 --> 00:46:55,959
Hey.

660
00:47:02,716 --> 00:47:04,509
I'll send someone. Stay out of sight!

661
00:47:11,058 --> 00:47:11,934
Fuck this!

662
00:47:21,693 --> 00:47:22,611
Hey, it's me.

663
00:47:22,694 --> 00:47:26,114
I left a guy who'd been shot
on the mountain road to Manbulam.

664
00:47:26,198 --> 00:47:27,366
Take him and save him.

665
00:47:27,950 --> 00:47:29,368
Hey, hurry up!

666
00:47:29,451 --> 00:47:31,995
You have to save him no matter what.
Got it?

667
00:48:07,239 --> 00:48:08,865
Suspect vehicle confirmed.

668
00:48:15,622 --> 00:48:16,707
Follow him!

669
00:48:18,500 --> 00:48:22,045
Requesting confirmation
on a silver SUV near Manbulam. Over.

670
00:48:23,672 --> 00:48:24,506
Hey, block him!

671
00:48:34,975 --> 00:48:36,143
Suspect vehicle fleeing.

672
00:48:36,226 --> 00:48:38,311
Requesting patrol car at scene. Over.

673
00:48:41,356 --> 00:48:42,232
Chase him. Hurry!

674
00:48:50,824 --> 00:48:52,242
Entering Hwajeong Intersection.

675
00:48:54,870 --> 00:48:58,248
Suspect vehicle direction confirmed.
Will block escape route.

676
00:49:14,097 --> 00:49:19,019
Suspect vehicle fleeing toward town.
All units assist. Over.

677
00:49:48,465 --> 00:49:49,382
Shit!

678
00:50:01,019 --> 00:50:02,896
Suspect vehicle is in the alley!

679
00:50:13,615 --> 00:50:14,658
Blocking escape route.

680
00:50:36,555 --> 00:50:38,348
Just ram it!

681
00:51:50,921 --> 00:51:52,631
PROVE IT. OR I'LL KILL YOU.

682
00:51:52,714 --> 00:51:54,216
"Uncle."

683
00:51:54,966 --> 00:51:56,176
"Han Hui-su."

684
00:52:05,685 --> 00:52:06,895
It's a pretty big amount.

685
00:52:07,604 --> 00:52:08,730
I know, right?

686
00:52:32,087 --> 00:52:34,422
Here…

687
00:52:35,423 --> 00:52:36,258
Here…

688
00:52:38,969 --> 00:52:39,844
Here…

689
00:58:00,164 --> 00:58:03,084
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang

